.Dd September 13, 2026
.Dt ZKEYS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zkeys
.Nd retrieve secrets from a zkeys service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm get-key
.Op Fl -config-file Ar file
.Ar name
.Nm
.Cm help
.Op Ar command
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
retrieves secrets from a zkeys service and is designed for integration with
ZFS deployments to securely unlock pools or file systems without keeping the
key stored on the same machine.
.Pp
Note that, by design, this client does
.Em not
support administrative key operations such as key unlocking.
This is to prevent mistakes resulting in ever storing privileged credentials on
the machine as that would defeat the purpose of the remote service's auto-key
locking features.
.Ss The get-key command
The get-key command retrieves the secret for the key named by
.Ar name .
The name must identify a key in the configuration file.
The client authenticates to the service with the key's configured identifier
and remote password.
It prepends the configured local secret to the service response and writes the
result to standard output, followed by a newline.
.Pp
The following option is supported:
.Bl -tag -width XXXX
.It Fl -config-file Ar file
Path to the configuration file.
.Pp
Default:
.Pa @PREFIX@/etc/zkeys.toml
.El
.Ss The help command
The help command prints command-line usage information.
If
.Ar command
is given, it prints usage information for that command.
.Ss The version command
The version command prints the name of the package and its version to standard
output.
This command always exits successfully.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width XXXX
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/zkeys.toml
Default configuration file.
See
.Xr zkeys.toml 5
for its format.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zkeys.toml 5
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
package was developed by
.An Julio Merino
.Aq julio@meroh.net .
